 ### [Mapping Strategies](9321-mapping-strategies.md)
-Mapping strategies define the correspondence mechanism used to align pixels or features between two distinct scenes or frames for the purpose of fusion, editing, or SLAM initialization. They solve the problem of establishing spatial and semantic consistency when direct geometric alignment is ambiguous or unavailable. Unlike sibling methods that focus on the continuous representation of a single scene, mapping strategies specifically address the *inter-scene* or *inter-frame* registration step.
-*   **When to choose:** Use when fusing multiple independent reconstructions or initializing a SLAM system with sparse prior knowledge.
