 ### Active Mapping with 3D Gaussian Splatting
-Extends passive mapping with active view selection using Fisher Information [S5].
-*   **Steps:**
-    1.  Reconstruct environment using 3D Gaussians (e.g., via SplaTAM).
-    2.  Propose path candidates using frontier-based exploration.
-    3.  Sample cameras along the path concerning the mobility of the agent.
-    4.  Compute EIG for each path and choose the one with the highest EIG to continue exploration.
-*   **Formula:** $P_j = \arg \max_{P_j} \text{tr} \left( \sum_{x_{acq_i} \in P_j} H''[y_{i\_acq}|x_{acq_i}, w^*] \right) H''[w^*|D_{train}]^{-1}$ [S5].
-*   **When to choose:** Use for autonomous mapping where maximizing the information gain of new views is the primary objective.
